    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nRookery House is a charming and beautifully presented 4 bedroom detached residence, set amidst mature gardens extending to c. 0.35 acre and located within walking distance of the bustling centre of Killarney, one of Ireland's most popular tourist destinations. \nApproached by a long avenue and extensive front lawns planted with mature trees and shrubbery, Rookery House is a bright and spacious residence of c. 138.7 sq m, laid out over two floors. This home features two large reception rooms complete with period fireplaces, a bright and well-equipped kitchen, four bedrooms with ample storage and two bathrooms. \nRookery House is a classic detached residence, featuring a crisp white, perfectly symmetrical front façade complete with an elegant front porch. The sun-drenched stone patio immediately adjacent to the front porch is an ideal vantage point from which to enjoy the immaculately presented and private lawns surrounding the property. \nThe bright front porch leads to the inner hallway, where there is conveniently located understairs storage. Both spaces feature tasteful Victorian floor tiles. \n\nThe two reception rooms are located off the hall and both are of generous proportions. \nThe dining room features an attractive fireplace, with wooden surround and marble insert. There is access to the kitchen and downstairs bathroom off the dining room. \nThe living room is a sunny dual aspect room, featuring an antique Victorian style fireplace as the central focal of the room. \nThe kitchen is located to the rear of the property, from which there is access to the rear parking area. \nThe kitchen features pristine white cupboard doors complete with ornate handles and black countertops. The kitchen layout provides a sense of space and offers ample storage with floor level units and a pantry style, full-height cupboard. There is also a handy breakfast bar for busy mornings. The kitchen is plumbed for washing machine and the ground floor bathroom is a wet room. \nUpstairs there are four bedrooms, three of which are fitted with wardrobes and the fourth is fitted with bookshelves. There is also a family sized bathroom at this level too, featuring a bath. \nOutside\nResiding in a peaceful, tranquil location, with mountain views, Rookery House is an enchanting private oasis complemented by beautifully presented lawned areas and a tree lined driveway.\nThere is a garage/ shed located to the rear of the property which is brimming with future potential and suitable for future conversion (subject to planning).\nLocation\nThis excellent location offers residents a quiet, mature residential neighbourhood which is within walking distance of the vibrant town centre. The bustling heart of Killarney is just 1km from Rookery House giving you access to a host of famous restaurants, pubs and shops. The train station is also nearby, as is the bus station, providing superb access to public transport. For families, there are high regarded schools, both primary and secondary, in the immediate area and within walking distance of this stunning family home. \nKillarney maintains a bustling year-round hospitality scene as it features top-tier restaurants, traditional Irish music pubs, and the popular event space at the Gleneagle INEC Arena.\n\nThe locality is also is best described as a gateway to nature, with the beautiful Killarney National Park c. 1 km from this home. This park encompasses c. 25,000 acres of lakes, mountains and woodlands and residents and tourists alike enjoy the many hiking and cycling trails in the area. The world-renowned Ring of Kerry, with it's awe-inspiring natural environment and breath-taking scenery, is literally on your doorstep. \nEase of access to Cork and beyond is via the N22 and Kerry Airport is located c. 20 minutes' drive (17km) from the property, providing quick links to Dublin, the UK and Europe.\n\n Viewing: Strictly by prior appointment. \n\nJoint Selling Agents:\n\nTed Healy ASCSI ARICS Dip AVEA\nDNG Ted Healy\nE-mail: tedhealy@dng.ie\nTel: 064 6639000/ 087 6678315\n\nGemma Lanigan, BA MIPAV.\nDNG Country Homes & Estates,\nEmail: gemmalanigan@dng.ie\nTel: + 353 1 4912600/ + 353 87 4182967"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Porch - 2.36m x 1.71m\nTiled floor, large glazed windows overlooking front garden\n\nEntrance Hall - 1.59m x 5.62m\nTiled floor\n\nLiving Room - 4.17m x 5.12m\nTimber floor boards, open firplace, ceiling cornicing\n\nDining Room - 3.65m x 5.17m\nCarpeted, raised open fireplace with marble surround, ceiling cornicing\n\nKitchen - 3.66m x 3.71m\nTiled floor, fitted kitchen units, breakfast bar\n\nShower Room - 2.57m x 1.96m\nWalk in wet room, WC, WHB, Shower\n\nHalf Landing - 0.83m x 0.69m\nCarpeted stairs\n\nBedroom 4 - 2.4m x 3.24m\nCarpet, fitted wardrobe\n\nBathroom - 1.35m x 3.8m\nWC, WHB, Bath\n\nLanding - 1.57m x 3.93m\nCarpeted\n\nBedroom 1 - 4.05m x 5.14m\nCarpeted, fitted wardrobes\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.48m x 2.47m\nCarpeted, fitted wardobes\n\nBedroom 3 - 4.08m x 2.47m\nTimber floorboards, fitted book shelves\n\n"
